Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when freedesktop-sdk's python3-vcs-versioning.bst upstream carries ref-format: git-describe on its git_repo source.
Subject: python3-vcs-versioning: stage tag refs so sandbox git-describe returns

Same failure mode as python3-setuptools-scm (see 0004). The git_repo
source defaults to ref-format: sha1 and does not guarantee tag refs
are present in the staged clone. vcs-versioning's build hook runs

    git describe --dirty --tags --long --abbrev=40 --match 'vcs-versioning-*'

which walks the commit graph looking for a matching tag; with no tag
refs staged it exhausts setuptools-scm's default 40-second subprocess
timeout and fails the build (subprocess.TimeoutExpired).

Setting ref-format: git-describe instructs the plugin to stage the tag
refs so the sandbox git-describe returns in milliseconds. The element's
existing ref is already in git-describe format
(vcs-versioning-v2.6.0-0-gfa5c2319...), so this is consistent with how
the ref is stored.

Resolves: setuptools-scm#957.

diff --git a/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst b/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst
--- a/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst
+++ b/elements/components/python3-vcs-versioning.bst
@@ -17,5 +17,6 @@ variables:
 sources:
 - kind: git_repo
   url: github:pypa/setuptools_scm.git
+  ref-format: git-describe
   track: vcs-versioning-v*
   ref: vcs-versioning-v2.6.0-0-gfa5c2319fef46bea5e387e1329245e7eaffa6f1e
